&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;Both Houses of Parliament, the Lok Sabha and Rajya Sabha, on Saturday, October 3, reconstituted their department-related parliamentary standing committees for the year.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;Congress MP from Thiruvananthapuram Shashi Tharoor has been reappointed as chairman of the Parliamentary Committee on External Affairs. Several other chairpersons have also retained their positions, while a few committees have new heads.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tharoor, Anurag Thakur Retain Key Posts&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;Former Union minister and BJP Lok Sabha MP Anurag Thakur will continue as chairman of the Parliamentary Committee on Coal, Mines and Steel.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;&lt;iframe title=&quot;YouTube video player&quot; src=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/embed/_B9mMeQoXy0?si=xumfgrzpPQw2U_0u&quot; width=&quot;560&quot; height=&quot;315&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&

&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;Sheikh Hamdan bin Mohammed bin Rashid Al Maktoum, Deputy Prime Minister of the United Arab Emirates, called on flydubai pilot Smit Machchhar on Saturday and praised his &amp;ldquo;courage and responsibility&amp;rdquo; following the cockpit attack on a Dubai-Tel Aviv flight.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;Al Maktoum said Machchhar had &amp;ldquo;embodied high degrees of courage&amp;rdquo; and conveyed the UAE leadership&amp;rsquo;s &amp;ldquo;appreciation&amp;rdquo; to the Indian pilot.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;UAE Deputy PM Praises Machchhar&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;In a post on X, Al Maktoum shared a photograph from his visit to Machchhar and wrote, &amp;ldquo;During a visit to Captain Smit Machchhar&amp;hellip; the flydubai pilot who embodied the highest degrees of courage, responsibility, and care for human life.&amp;rdquo;&lt;/p&gt;
